---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'June 10, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Chord Sequence"
  description="Terms of Service for Chord Sequence. Free to use, no account required. Read our terms before using the app."
  canonicalUrl="https://chordsequence.com/terms/"
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Home</a>
      <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg>
      <span class="text-foreground">Terms of Service</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight mb-4">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence is a free, browser-based music tool. Use it to make music. Don't misuse it.
          We don't collect your personal data. Your work stays in your browser.
          That's pretty much it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Acceptance of terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using Chord Sequence at <strong class="text-foreground">chordsequence.com</strong>,
          you agree to these Terms of Service. If you don't agree, please don't use the service.
          These terms apply to all visitors and users of the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Use of the service</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">Chord Sequence is provided free of charge for personal and educational use. You may:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm mb-4">
          <li>Use the chord progression editor, bass tab player, tuner, metronome, and all other tools for any musical purpose</li>
          <li>Export your progressions and recordings as audio files (WAV) for use in your own projects</li>
          <li>Share links to the app or embed the URL in educational content</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-3">You may not:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li>Scrape, crawl, or systematically extract content from the site in a way that degrades service for other users</li>
          <li>Attempt to reverse-engineer, decompile, or exploit the app beyond normal browser usage</li>
          <li>Use the service for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable laws</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">User-submitted content</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Some features allow users to submit content — such as song charts added to the community library.
          By submitting content, you represent that:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <li>You have the right to share the content (e.g., chord charts are factual arrangements, not protected expression)</li>
          <li>The content does not infringe any third-party copyright, trademark, or intellectual property rights</li>
          <li>The content is accurate to the best of your knowledge</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We reserve the right to remove any submitted content at our discretion without notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          The Chord Sequence application, design, code, audio samples, and written content are owned by
          Elías Corsino Saldaña unless otherwise noted. All rights reserved.
        </p>
        <p>
          Music theory knowledge — scales, chord names, progressions, intervals — is not owned by anyone.
          The chord progressions you create with this tool are yours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">No warranties</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence is provided <strong class="text-foreground">"as is"</strong> without warranties of any kind,
          express or implied. We don't guarantee the service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or available
          at all times. Use it at your own discretion.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Chord Sequence and its creator shall not be liable for any
          indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from your use of — or inability
          to use — the service, including loss of data stored in your browser.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence is hosted on <strong class="text-foreground">Netlify</strong> and uses
          <strong class="text-foreground">Supabase</strong> for the community song library database.
          Your use of those services is subject to their respective terms and privacy policies.
          We are not responsible for the practices of third-party services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms of Service from time to time. Changes take effect when published on this page.
          The effective date at the top will be updated accordingly. Continued use of the service after changes
          constitutes acceptance of the new terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Dominican Republic, without regard to conflict of law principles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? Reach us at
          <a href="mailto:corsinoelias@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">corsinoelias@gmail.com</a>
          or through our <a href="/contact/" class="text-primary hover:underline">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
